use std
into ragdoll.amni

The `ragdoll` library: an `anim` skeleton as physics bodies joined by limited spherical joints; namespace ragdoll, imports math, vec, physics, anim.math and anim.pose. Every number is f32. Already provided and never defined here, in namespace anim: `Skeleton` (n, parent with -1 for the root, rest_t, rest_r, rest_s; always passed by reference), `Pose` (n and arrays t, r, s; by reference), `Model` (n and array x of `Xf`; by reference), `Xf` (t float3, r float4 quaternion x y z w, s float3), `xf_mul(a, b)`, `xf_inv(a)`, `xf_point(x, p)`, `qmul`, `qconj`, `qrot(q, v)`, `qnorm`, `qfromto(a, b)` and `QI`; in namespace physics `World`, `Body`, `SphericalJoint`, `Quat` (x, y, z, w), `Transform` (p, q), `Capsule` (center1, center2, radius), `Sphere` (center, radius), `DYNAMIC`, `default_body_def()` (fields body_type, position, rotation, linear_damping, angular_damping), `default_shape_def()` (fields density, `material.friction`, `filter.group_index`), `default_spherical_joint_def()` (field `base` with body_a, body_b, frame_a, frame_b, collide_connected; and enable_cone_limit, cone_angle, enable_twist_limit, lower_twist_angle, upper_twist_angle, enable_spring, hertz, damping_ratio, target_rotation), `create_body(world, def) Body`, `create_capsule_shape(body, def, capsule)`, `create_sphere_shape(body, def, sphere)`, `create_spherical_joint(world, def) SphericalJoint`, `position(body)`, `rotation(body) Quat`, `set_transform(body, p, q)`, `set_linear_velocity(body, v)`, `set_angular_velocity(body, v)`, `cone_angle(joint)`, `twist_angle(joint)`, `enable_cone_limit(joint, on)`, `set_cone_limit(joint, angle)`, `enable_twist_limit(joint, on)`, `set_twist_limits(joint, lo, hi)`, `enable_spring(joint, on)`, `set_spring_hertz(joint, hz)` and `set_target_rotation(joint, q)`.

`pq(q float4) physics::Quat` and `fq(q physics::Quat) float4` copy x, y, z, w across.

`Settings` holds thickness 0.2, min_radius 0.02, max_radius 0.17, density 1000, friction 0.7, cone 0.7, twist 0.5, linear_damping 0.07, angular_damping 0.7, group -7, self_collide false, mass_ratio 3 and inertia_scale 3; `settings()` returns them.

`Ragdoll` holds `w` (the world), `n` (joint count), growable arrays with one entry per skeleton joint: `bodies` (Body), `joints` (SphericalJoint, unused for the root), `jointed` (bool, false for a root), `fb` (float4, the joint frame's rotation in the joint's own body), `cone`, `lo`, `hi` (its limits), `lens` and `radii` (f32), and `limited` (bool, whether limits are on).

`build(w, sk, m, at, s, radii) Ragdoll` makes one dynamic body per joint j, in index order (a parent always comes before its children). Its world transform W is `xf_mul(at, m.x[j])`; the body sits at W.t with rotation W.r, with the settings' damping. The bone axis in world space goes from W.t to the mean world position of the joint's children; when it has none, or that axis is shorter than 1e-3, the joint is a leaf and its axis is the direction from its parent's world position to W.t (straight up for a lone root), with length 0. `lens[j]` is that length. The local axis a is `qrot(qconj(W.r), axis)` normalized. The radius is radii[j] when j is inside the radii slice and that value is above 0; otherwise for a bone clamp(length × thickness, min_radius, max_radius) and for a leaf clamp(the parent's length × 0.35, min_radius, max_radius) (or max_radius for a lone root). The shape def has the settings' density and friction and group index 0 when self_collide, else the settings' group. A bone longer than twice the radius gets a capsule from a × radius to a × (length - radius); a shorter bone gets a sphere of that radius at a × max(length / 2, radius); a leaf gets a sphere at a × radius. `fb[j]` is `qfromto((0, 0, 1), a)`. Each joint with a parent p gets a spherical joint from p's body (body_a) to this body (body_b), collide_connected false, frame_a at `qrot(qconj(Wp.r), W.t - Wp.t)` with rotation `qmul(sk.rest_r[j], fb[j])` and frame_b at the origin with rotation `fb[j]` (both converted with `pq`), so the relative rotation is identity at the rest pose and the twist axis runs along the bone; cone and twist limits on with cone angle s.cone and twist -s.twist to s.twist, recorded in cone, lo and hi; the spring starts off with hertz 0 and damping ratio 1. `limited` starts true. Then the bodies are made stiffer to spin and balanced, since a light or thin body between heavy ones lets joint limits give way. Raising a body's mass to m multiplies its mass and every inertia column by m over its mass; raising its inertia to t multiplies only the inertia columns by t over its inertia trace (the sum of the diagonal); both keep the center, go through `physics::mass_data` and `physics::set_mass_data`, and do nothing when the body already has at least that much. First every body's inertia is raised to its own trace × inertia_scale. Then in index order every jointed body has its mass raised to its parent's mass / mass_ratio and then its inertia raised to its parent's inertia trace / mass_ratio; then in reverse index order every jointed body's parent has its mass raised to the child's mass / mass_ratio and its inertia raised to the child's inertia trace / mass_ratio.

`limit(rd, j, cone, lo, hi)` with rd by reference records and sets new limits on joint j when it is jointed. `use_limits(rd, on)` turns every joint's cone and twist limits on or off and records it.

`start(rd, sk, m0, m1, at0, at1, dt)` hands animation over: for every joint, W0 = `xf_mul(at0, m0.x[j])` and W1 = `xf_mul(at1, m1.x[j])`; the body is placed at W1; its linear velocity is (W1.t - W0.t) / dt; its angular velocity comes from d = `qmul(W1.r, qconj(W0.r))` (negated when d.w is below 0): angle 2 × acos(min(d.w, 1)), and when the length of (d.x, d.y, d.z) is above 1e-7 the velocity is that vector normalized times angle / dt, else zero.

`read(rd, sk, at, out)` writes the bodies back into the pose `out` (by reference): out.n is sk.n. With ia = `xf_inv(at)`, every joint's model rotation is `qnorm(qmul(ia.r, fq(rotation)))` of its body and its model position `xf_point(ia, position)`. For each joint, out.r is the model rotation for the root and `qnorm(qmul(qconj(parent's model rotation), own))` otherwise; out.t is the model position for the root and sk.rest_t[j] otherwise; out.s is sk.rest_s[j].

`drive(rd, sk, target, hz)` powers the joints toward the target pose: for every jointed j, when hz is above 0 enable the spring, set its hertz to hz and its target rotation to `pq` of `qmul(qmul(qconj(qmul(sk.rest_r[j], fb[j])), target.r[j]), fb[j])`; otherwise disable the spring.

`violation(rd) f32` is the worst amount any jointed joint is past its limits: max(0, `cone_angle` - cone) and, for twist, max(0, lo - `twist_angle`) and max(0, `twist_angle` - hi), largest over all joints (0 when nothing is past).
